  "limitations": [
    "One fresh direct Telnet process records B/C/D, the shrunk pre-write body, one CUP 12;1 RESIZED action, then the restored endpoint; direct Telnet is protocol/display evidence only.",
    "The initial body places B/C/D at source rows 7/9/10; the fixed 80x24 -> 60x12 shrink follows.",
    "Four stages preserve the pre-write body and post-write endpoint; only phases 1 and 3 resize, while phase 2 sends the exact declared CUP+RESIZED bytes.",
    "Document markers, protocol DSR, caret API and visible rectangles remain different observations; no internal storage or addressing policy is inferred.",
    "The finite text allowlist admits the fixed CUP 12;1 RESIZED prefix overwrite without predicting the actually affected row.",
    "Only 80x24 -> 60x12 -> 80x24 with fixed ASCII is covered; no full grid, styles, local-shell/native-grid transport, alternate screen, reliability repetition or performance acceptance.",
    "Raw document text, paths, process identifiers, profiles, resources and provider diagnostics remain private."
  ]
